{"name":"Roanoke","hex":"#372b25","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Roanoke","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A placename:\n Ellipsis of Roanoke Colony: a failed late 16th century English former colony on what is now the coast of North Carolina in the United States.","Ellipsis of Roanoke Colony: a failed late 16th century English former colony on what is now the coast of North Carolina in the United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Roanoke"}],"entries":[{"title":"Roanoke Colony","blocks":[{"text":"The Roanoke Colony was the site of two attempts by Sir Walter Raleigh to found the first permanent English settlement in North America. The first colony was established at Roanoke Island in 1585 as a military outpost, and was evacuated in 1586. The more famous second colony, known as the Lost Colony, began when a new group of settlers under John White arrived on the island in 1587; a ship in 1590 found the colony abandoned."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/William_Ludwell_Sheppard_%26_William_James_Linton_-_CROATOAN%2C_The_Lost_Colony_%28John_White%29.jpg/330px-William_Ludwell_Sheppard_%26_William_James_Linton_-_CROATOAN%2C_The_Lost_Colony_%28John_White%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roanoke_Colony"},{"title":"Roanoke Island","blocks":[{"text":"Roanoke Island is an island in Dare County, bordered by the Outer Banks of North Carolina. It was named after the historical Roanoke, a Carolina Algonquian people who inhabited the area in the 16th century at the time of English colonization."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Roanoke_NASA_World_Wind.jpg/330px-Roanoke_NASA_World_Wind.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roanoke_Island"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia